. /*=========================================================================*/
. *---1. The exhibits and what to look for in each---*
. * One entry per output file. Each note says what should match the paper and where we
. * know ours differs, so a quick look tells you whether it came out right.
. /*=========================================================================*/
. 
. *--- figures
. local figs figure1_grade5 figure1_grade4 figure2_grade5 figure2_grade4

. 
. local title_figure1_grade5 "Figure I, grade 5"

. local title_figure1_grade4 "Figure I, grade 4"

. local title_figure2_grade5 "Figure II, grade 5"

. local title_figure2_grade4 "Figure II, grade 4"

. 
. local look_figure1_grade5 "Actual class size should follow the dashed rule and drop sharply just past 40, 80 and 120, by less than the rule says. 
> Ours starts at enrollment 8, not 5, because we drop the one school at 5, and we leave out the paper's horizontal lines."

. local look_figure1_grade4 "Same pattern as grade 5. Actual class size tracks the dashed rule and drops just past 40, 80 and 120. We leave out the 
> paper's horizontal lines."

. local look_figure2_grade5 "Scores should rise with enrollment overall and dip where predicted class size peaks, roughly a mirror image of the dash
> ed line. The end points can differ, our first point keeps enrollments 5 to 9 and our last stops at 169, where the paper starts at 9 and pools 160 
> to 190."

. local look_figure2_grade4 "Same reading as grade 5, scores dip where predicted class size peaks. The end points can differ for the same reason as 
> grade 5."

. 
. *--- tables, each with the paper table it matches
. local tabs table1 table2 table2_se table3_full table3_disc5 table4 table5 table6

. 
. local paper_table1       table1

. local paper_table2       table2

. local paper_table2_se    table2

. local paper_table3_full  table3

. local paper_table3_disc5 table3

. local paper_table4       table4

. local paper_table5       table5

. local paper_table6       table6

. 
. local title_table1       "Table I, descriptive statistics"

. local title_table2       "Table II, OLS"

. local title_table2_se    "Table II, column (2), three standard errors (the required addition)"

. local title_table3_full  "Table III, reduced forms, full sample (the paper's panel A)"

. local title_table3_disc5 "Table III, reduced forms, +/-5 sample (the paper's panel B)"

. local title_table4       "Table IV, 2SLS, grade 5"

. local title_table5       "Table V, 2SLS, grade 4"

. local title_table6       "Table VI, dummy instruments, +/-5 and +/-3 samples"

. 
. local look_table1       "Means, s.d. and quantiles by grade, with the class and school counts in each panel header. There is no grade 3 panel beca
> use the grade 3 data isn't provided."

. local look_table2       "Class size is positive alone and close to zero once percent disadvantaged is added. Our standard errors are clustered by 
> school while the paper's are corrected for within-school correlation, so they differ a little."

. local look_table2_se    "The paper has no table like this. It is the required comparison of three standard errors for column (2), shown against th
> e paper's Table II."

. local look_table3_full  "In the class size columns fsc is the first stage, large and positive. In the score columns fsc is the reduced form, mostl
> y negative."

. local look_table3_disc5 "The same models on the +/-5 sample, with far fewer classes, so the standard errors are bigger."

. local look_table4       "Class size should be negative in the reading columns and in most math columns. Columns 5 and 6 and 11 and 12 use the +/-5
>  sample."

. local look_table5       "Same layout as Table IV for grade 4. The effects are smaller than in grade 5."

. local look_table6       "Each block is the +/-5 sample with percent disadvantaged, then the +/-3 sample with and without it, as in the paper."

. 
. 
. /*=========================================================================*/
. *---2. Which exhibits did this run produce---*
. * confirm file sets _rc to 0 when the file is there.
. /*=========================================================================*/
. 
. local nfig = 0

. foreach f in `figs' {
  2.     capture confirm file "$root/output/`f'.png"
  3.     local made_`f' = (_rc == 0)                     // 1 if the figure is there
  4.     local nfig = `nfig' + `made_`f''
  5. }

. local ntab = 0

. foreach t in `tabs' {
  2.     capture confirm file "$root/output/`t'.tex"
  3.     local made_`t' = (_rc == 0)                     // 1 if the table is there
  4.     local ntab = `ntab' + `made_`t''
  5. }

. local nfigs : word count `figs'

. local ntabs : word count `tabs'

. 
. 
. /*=========================================================================*/
. *---3. Write the page---*
. * Plain HTML written line by line with file write. Figures sit side by side with the
. * paper's. Tables are .tex files, which a browser can't show, so each one is read in as
. * text, stripped of its LaTeX commands, and written out as an HTML table above the scan
. * of the paper's table.
. /*=========================================================================*/
. 
. file open chk using "$root/figure_check/figure_check.html", write replace

. file write chk "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Figure and table check</title>" _n

. file write chk "<style>body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;margin:24px;max-width:1400px}" _n

. file write chk ".row{display:flex;gap:16px}.row div{flex:1}img{max-width:100%;border:1px solid #ccc}" _n

. file write chk ".ok{color:#1a7f37;font-weight:bold}.miss{color:#c62828;font-weight:bold}.note{color:#444}h2{margin-top:36px}" _n

. file write chk ".wrap{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;margin-bottom:12px}" _n

. file write chk "table.tex{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}table.tex td{padding:2px 8px;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}" _n

. file write chk "table.tex td:first-child{text-align:left}tr.rule td{border-top:1px solid #000;padding:0;height:2px}</style></head><body>" _n

. file write chk "<h1>Figure and table check</h1>" _n

. file write chk "<p>Run on `c(current_date)' at `c(current_time)'. <b>`nfig' of `nfigs'</b> figures and <b>`ntab' of `ntabs'</b> tables produced in
>  this run.</p>" _n

. 
. *--- figures, ours on the left, the paper's on the right
. foreach f in `figs' {
  2.     file write chk "<h2>`title_`f''</h2>" _n
  3.     if `made_`f'' file write chk "<p class='ok'>PASS, output/`f'.png was produced</p>" _n
  4.     else file write chk "<p class='miss'>MISSING, output/`f'.png was not produced</p>" _n
  5.     file write chk "<div class='row'><div><b>Ours</b><br><img src='../output/`f'.png'></div>" _n
  6.     file write chk "<div><b>Angrist and Lavy</b><br><img src='paper/`f'.png'></div></div>" _n
  7.     file write chk "<p class='note'>`look_`f''</p>" _n
  8. }

. 
. *--- tables, ours on top, the paper's underneath
. foreach t in `tabs' {
  2.     file write chk "<h2>`title_`t''</h2>" _n
  3.     if `made_`t'' {
  4.         file write chk "<p class='ok'>PASS, output/`t'.tex was produced</p>" _n
  5. 
.         * read the .tex in, one line per row of data
.         quietly infix str2045 line 1-2045 using "$root/output/`t'.tex", clear
  6.         quietly {
  7.             replace line = strtrim(line)
  8.             gen byte rule = inlist(line, char(92) + "toprule", char(92) + "midrule", char(92) + "bottomrule")
  9.             * drop the LaTeX-only lines (begin, end, def, addlinespace, lone braces), keep table rows
.             drop if line == "" | line == "{" | line == "}"
 10.             drop if substr(line, 1, 1) == char(92) & !rule & strpos(line, "multicolumn") == 0
 11.             * strip the LaTeX commands and keep the text, char(92) is a backslash
.             replace line = ustrregexra(line, "multicolumn\{[0-9]+\}\{[lcr]\}", "")
 12.             replace line = subinstr(line, "sym", "", .)
 13.             replace line = subinstr(line, "footnotesize", "", .)
 14.             replace line = subinstr(line, char(92), "", .)
 15.             replace line = subinstr(line, "{", "", .)
 16.             replace line = subinstr(line, "}", "", .)
 17.             * make the text safe for HTML, then turn each & into a new cell
.             replace line = subinstr(line, "&", "|c|", .)
 18.             replace line = subinstr(line, "<", "&lt;", .)
 19.             replace line = subinstr(line, ">", "&gt;", .)
 20.             replace line = subinstr(line, "|c|", "</td><td>", .)
 21.             replace line = "<tr><td>" + line + "</td></tr>" if !rule
 22.             replace line = "<tr class='rule'><td colspan='13'></td></tr>" if rule
 23.         }
 24.         file write chk "<b>Ours</b><div class='wrap'><table class='tex'>" _n
 25.         forvalues i = 1/`=_N' {
 26.             file write chk (line[`i']) _n
 27.         }
 28.         file write chk "</table></div>" _n
 29.     }
 30.     else file write chk "<p class='miss'>MISSING, output/`t'.tex was not produced</p>" _n
 31.     file write chk "<b>Angrist and Lavy</b><br><img src='paper/`paper_`t''.png'>" _n
 32.     file write chk "<p class='note'>`look_`t''</p>" _n
 33. }

. 
. file write chk "</body></html>" _n

. file close chk

. 
. *--- the same result in the log
. display _n "Check, `nfig' of `nfigs' figures and `ntab' of `ntabs' tables produced, see figure_check/figure_check.html"

Check, 4 of 4 figures and 8 of 8 tables produced, see figure_check/figure_check.html

. if `nfig' < `nfigs' | `ntab' < `ntabs' display as error "At least one exhibit is missing, check figure_check/figure_check.html and the logs"

. 
. 
